<%/* A map of the project's parts, with some marked: the design system's map
     (components/map.html, guideline 13), printed from its model. Two things
     draw one:
       - a prelude-map-1 block the agent wrote: the parts it names are
         outlined (.named), each with its note, and nothing is said about
         change, since the block can't say whether it proposes one or only
         explains (the person, 2026-10-23);
       - Prelude itself, after a turn that changed the app's code: the parts
         whose files changed (.touched, "Changed"), no agent involved.
     It's the whole map, as the architecture of the session's branch has it
     now. The parts it leaves alone step back to their names, so a chat
     column holds it. Each part links to its page in the architecture.

     With no mark it's the plain map, every part with its summary, as the
     Architecture page draws it (views shares this partial).

     The model, ready to print: label (the map's name), mark ('touched',
     'named' or none), count (parts marked), and layers, each with title
     and parts (id, title, url, summary, outside, marked, note); `target`,
     if given, is the region a part's page opens in (the chat's drawer; the
     Architecture page gives none, so its parts open as pages). */%>
<% const parts = n => n === 1 ? '1 part' : `${n} parts`;
   const said = it.mark === 'touched' ? `${parts(it.count)} changed. ` : ''; %>
<figure class="stack gap-2">
  <div class="map" aria-label="<%= it.label %>">
    <% for (const layer of it.layers) { %>
    <section class="map-layer" aria-label="<%= layer.title %>">
      <h3 class="map-label"><%= layer.title %></h3>
      <ul class="map-nodes">
        <% for (const part of layer.parts) { %>
        <li><a class="map-node<%= part.outside ? ' outside' : '' %><%= part.marked ? ` ${it.mark}` : '' %>" href="<%= part.url %>"<% if (it.target) { %> ko-target="<%= it.target %>"<% } %>>
          <span class="map-node-title"><%= part.title %><% if (part.marked && it.mark === 'touched') { %><span class="pill accent">Changed</span><% } %></span>
          <% if (part.marked || !it.mark) { %><span class="muted"><%= part.note ?? part.summary %></span><% } %>
        </a></li>
        <% } %>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <% } %>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="muted"><%= said %>Read from the top: each part uses parts in its own layer or below it.</figcaption>
</figure>
